From: Matt Ficken <mattficken@php.net>
Date: Mon, 15 May 2017 02:21:55 -0700
Subject: fixing run-tests.php for variables_order="GPCS"

PHP 7.0 never got this change (PHP 7.2.0). Its run-tests.php takes the
environment of the tests from $_ENV, which is empty when the PHP that runs
it reads a php.ini with variables_order = "GPCS" (php.ini-production in
/etc/php/7.0/cli on a machine with php7.0-cli installed): the tests then
run without SKIP_ONLINE_TESTS, SKIP_IO_CAPTURE_TESTS and HOME. Only the
fallback is taken, and it is adapted: getenv() without arguments returns
the environment only as of PHP 7.1, so the variables are taken from
$_SERVER, where the CLI registers them as well, and checked with getenv().

(cherry picked from commit c1d57186976e75a2a54f7bd167a77e2872cadc6a)
---
 run-tests.php | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/run-tests.php b/run-tests.php
index 333b517..34e64b7 100755
--- a/run-tests.php
+++ b/run-tests.php
@@ -131,6 +131,17 @@ SAFE_MODE_WARNING;
 }
 
 $environment = isset($_ENV) ? $_ENV : array();
+// Note: php.ini-development sets variables_order="GPCS" not "EGPCS", in which case $_ENV is NOT populated.
+//       detect and handle this case, or die or warn
+if (empty($environment)) {
+	// getenv() returns all environment variables only as of PHP 7.1,
+	// so take them from $_SERVER, where the CLI registers them too
+	foreach ($_SERVER as $name => $value) {
+		if (is_string($value) && getenv($name) === $value) {
+			$environment[$name] = $value;
+		}
+	}
+}
 if ((substr(PHP_OS, 0, 3) == "WIN") && empty($environment["SystemRoot"])) {
   $environment["SystemRoot"] = getenv("SystemRoot");
 }
